00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:23.350
being the only woman in the house?

00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:25.000
How's that?

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.050
- I think she's fine with it

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:28.189
cause she's not there very often.

00:00:28.189 --> 00:00:29.660
- [Derek] Oh! (laughs)

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:31.690
- [Alan] So we moved to
Florida a little while ago,

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:32.523
right?
- [Derek] Okay.

00:00:32.523 --> 00:00:33.356
- [Alan] So we're down in the South.

00:00:33.356 --> 00:00:35.350
And not Miami, we're like deep south.

00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:36.183
- [Derek] Right.
- Alabama-ish.

00:00:36.183 --> 00:00:37.016
- Oh wow!

00:00:37.016 --> 00:00:40.190
- And we are in like the
Bermuda triangle of Costco's.

00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:42.080
We're two hours from every Costco.

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:43.910
And there's like one to the north.

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:45.870
So she has like her weekly Costco run,

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:47.030
and she'll be gone for days!

00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:47.863
- Really? (laughs)

00:00:47.863 --> 00:00:49.230
- And it's just me and the boys.

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:50.961
I'm just refereeing their fist fights.

00:00:50.961 --> 00:00:51.794
- [Derek] Right.

00:00:51.794 --> 00:00:52.950
- And we do the best we can.

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:54.970
And then we get fed when she comes home.

00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:56.310
- [Derek] You actually posted a video,

00:00:56.310 --> 00:00:59.519
I saw that of a plumbing emergency,

00:00:59.519 --> 00:01:00.988
- [Alan] Oh yeah!
- Where some of the boys,

00:01:00.988 --> 00:01:02.034
let's take a look at that right now.

00:01:02.034 --> 00:01:03.225
- [Alan] Yeah.

00:01:03.225 --> 00:01:04.857
- [Alan] Oh my gosh!

00:01:04.857 --> 00:01:06.010
What the heck?

00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:07.070
Oh my gosh!

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:08.177
Is there a poop in there right now?

00:01:08.177 --> 00:01:09.190
- [Son] No.

00:01:09.190 --> 00:01:10.241
- [Alan ] Did you pee?

00:01:10.241 --> 00:01:11.507
- [Son] I didn't poop or pee.

00:01:11.507 --> 00:01:12.910
I was just gonna go poop.

00:01:12.910 --> 00:01:13.981
- [Alan] Oh my gosh!

00:01:13.981 --> 00:01:15.480
- [Woman] Is guess
(indistinct) taking a shower?

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:18.410
- [Alan] Oh my gosh! Oh my gosh.

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:19.953
- [Son] All the pee!

00:01:19.953 --> 00:01:21.660
- [Alan] Everybody grab a pair of shoes.

00:01:21.660 --> 00:01:23.710
- [Derek] That is, oh my gosh!

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:25.190
- Yeah, we did save those shoes.

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:26.120
That's the important thing.

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:28.440
- [Derek] Did you guys figure
out which boy did it or?

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:31.410
- You know, I know that
my oldest now has a sign

00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:32.550
on his bedroom door that says

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:34.710
'Warning Toxic Fumes' inside.

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:36.570
So I think,

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:38.310
I think it has something
to do with the him.

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:39.230
- [Derek] Right! So he's like,

00:01:39.230 --> 00:01:40.063
- [Alan] Yes! There it is.

00:01:40.063 --> 00:01:41.530
- [Derek] I may or may
not have done this father.

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:43.060
- Yeah.

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:44.980
I think those pipes are still
running to this day though.

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:47.330
That was a, that was we were
on like a farm in Toronto

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:48.310
where we shot Reacher.

00:01:48.310 --> 00:01:49.143
- [Derek] Oh my gosh.

00:01:49.143 --> 00:01:52.540
- And we told the landlord that
there was sewage everywhere.

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:53.527
And they were like,

00:01:53.527 --> 00:01:55.530
"Oh, we'll get somebody out
there pretty soon there eh!."

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:58.433
And like three weeks later,
I'm still like mopping up the,

00:01:58.433 --> 00:02:00.080
Anyway.
- Oh my gosh, man.

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:03.050
Now, so speaking of you're
in Toronto filming, right?

00:02:03.050 --> 00:02:04.060
- [Alan] That's right.
- Filming Reacher.

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:05.830
- So it's, it's called Reacher.

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:08.120
And it's based off the
books, Jack Reacher,

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:09.730
and also the movies with Tom cruise in it.

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:11.310
Can you tell us a little
bit about the show?

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:13.350
- Sure. Yeah. So if you
haven't read the books,

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:15.330
Lee Child's brilliant Reacher series

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:18.200
is about a former military police officer.

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:19.530
He was a detective in the military,

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:21.770
and now he's retired, and
he just kind of wanders.

00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:22.770
He's a hobo.
- Wow.

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:24.370
- [Alan] Nothing but a
toothbrush and a passport.

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:26.580
But you know with a
skillset like he's got,

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:29.010
he can't help but seek
justice wherever he goes.

00:02:29.010 --> 00:02:30.760
So, you know, trouble seems to find him.

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:31.810
- [Derek] Trouble seems to find him.

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:33.950
I, I, so I actually,

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:35.376
I watched the first
episode the other night.

00:02:35.376 --> 00:02:36.209
- Oh yeah!

00:02:36.209 --> 00:02:37.590
What did you think?

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:38.790
- [Derek] I loved it man. I loved it.

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:39.623
First thing I said,

00:02:39.623 --> 00:02:41.510
honestly I may or may not
have done a few pushups

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:42.343
and sit-ups as I was watching it.

00:02:42.343 --> 00:02:43.660
- Okay. (laughs) Fair enough.

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:44.493
- [Derek] And my girlfriend walked in,

00:02:44.493 --> 00:02:45.326
and she was like, "What are you doing?",

00:02:45.326 --> 00:02:47.090
I was like, " Have you seen this guy?".

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:48.120
Oh my gosh!

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:49.617
So you bulked up for this role.

00:02:49.617 --> 00:02:50.603
Quite a bit!
- [Alan] I did!

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:51.436
I did, yeah.

00:02:51.436 --> 00:02:52.367
Yeah, I usually walk around at like 205.

00:02:52.367 --> 00:02:53.270
(crowd applauds)

00:02:53.270 --> 00:02:54.760
Yeah. Thanks guys.

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:55.593
Thanks.

00:02:55.593 --> 00:02:56.426
- [Derek] Oh my gosh.

00:02:56.426 --> 00:02:57.259
See you later ladies and
gentlemen, I'm out of here!

00:02:57.259 --> 00:02:58.092
(Alan laughs)

00:02:58.092 --> 00:02:58.925
Oh my God!

00:02:58.925 --> 00:03:00.707
- Cause I want to be average.
I want to be average.

00:03:00.707 --> 00:03:01.540
You know, I'm an actor,

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:02.960
I've gotta be able to play like the dad,

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:04.820
and doctor, and the superhero, you know?

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:06.150
Whatever comes by.

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:08.480
No but yeah, I put on 30 pounds, which is,

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:09.320
I don't know if you've ever done.

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:10.510
Have you ever put on 30 pounds?

00:03:10.510 --> 00:03:11.730
- [Derek] No.

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:13.167
I don't even know if I
weighed 30 pounds honestly.

00:03:13.167 --> 00:03:16.930
- It's (laughs) It's a
full-time job to eat enough,

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:17.970
- [Derek] Wow.
- To put on 30 pounds.

00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:20.480
I had an assistant whose only
job was to bring me food.

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:23.340
It was like a conveyor belt
of smoothies and protein.

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:24.730
- [Derek] What does that
look like as far as like

00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:27.290
how many times in a day?

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:28.164
- Hundreds!

00:03:28.164 --> 00:03:28.997
- [Derek] Really?

00:03:28.997 --> 00:03:29.953
- You know, but, you know,

00:03:29.953 --> 00:03:31.710
you can get pretty clever with this.

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:33.760
I would order the crew,

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:35.890
like Popeye's chicken sandwiches,

00:03:35.890 --> 00:03:39.836
cookies, just so I could get
the kind of calories I wanted.

00:03:39.836 --> 00:03:42.160
It looks like a good will gesture.

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:43.130
- Wow.
(audience laughing)

00:03:43.130 --> 00:03:43.963
- [Alan] You know?

00:03:43.963 --> 00:03:46.380
Leave a dozen of those
in my trailer please.

00:03:46.380 --> 00:03:47.680
Hashtag that.

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:49.210
- [Derek] Before we go,

00:03:49.210 --> 00:03:51.960
you support something
called The Heart and,

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:53.770
The Heart and Armor Foundation.

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:54.603
- That's right.

00:03:54.603 --> 00:03:55.436
- [Derek] Can you tell
a little bit about that?

00:03:55.436 --> 00:03:57.093
- Yeah. So, you know,

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:01.680
we found each other at the right time.

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:03.400
I had like an early midlife crisis.

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:04.510
You know, I was depressed

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:07.140
and trying to find purpose and meaning.

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:09.510
My parents were, are both
veterans in the military.

00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:10.630
- [Derek] Wow.

00:04:10.630 --> 00:04:13.030
- You know, so I have a
heart for the service members

00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:13.863
in the country

00:04:13.863 --> 00:04:15.910
And you know, what people
don't realize is it's

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:17.380
the 1% serving the 99.

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:20.590
So not many of us can relate
to the kind of experiences

00:04:20.590 --> 00:04:21.900
that they have, right?

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:24.470
But these are people who
need care and consideration.

00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:26.400
And the Heart and Armor Foundation

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:28.070
is one that focuses on science.

00:04:28.070 --> 00:04:30.450
So it's not sexy or glamorous,

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:33.070
but they do they do research that matters.

00:04:33.070 --> 00:04:35.530
They'll study food
insecurity for veterans,

00:04:35.530 --> 00:04:40.390
PTSD, women's health,
and reproductive health,

00:04:40.390 --> 00:04:43.240
mental health in the armed services.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:45.700
So, you know, it's really important work.

00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:47.770
And I think, hopefully that science

00:04:47.770 --> 00:04:50.050
sort of makes us way to
the rest of us, you know?

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:52.820
So we'll all benefit as we
normally do by their service.

00:04:52.820 --> 00:04:54.140
So yeah, it's a good work.

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:56.130
Check them out at Heart
and Armor Foundation.

00:04:56.130 --> 00:04:58.110
You know, they could
always use the support

00:04:58.110 --> 00:05:00.170
to help fund the next study.

00:05:00.170 --> 00:05:01.560
- [Derek] Absolutely
man. That's beautiful.

00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:02.393
(audience applauds)

00:05:02.393 --> 00:05:03.840
Thank you so much for being here Alan.

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:06.247
- Thank you!
- [Derek] You're the best man!

